  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: JxPath\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: JxPath\n       Program: commons-jxpath\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JxPath/JxPath.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-jxpath.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JxPath/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 22\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: JxPath-19\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n7b2847e882a9e4216dcf0f35d27101e363611532\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2010-02-27 18:34:39 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nJXPATH-125\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/JXPATH-125\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.AliasedNamespaceIterationTest::testIterateJDOM\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Evaluating pointer iterator </a:doc/a:elem> expected:<[/a:doc[1]/a:elem[1], /a:doc[1]/a:elem[2]]> but was:<[/a:doc[1]/a:elem[1], /a:doc[1]/a:elem[1]]>\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.AliasedNamespaceIterationTest::testIterateDOM\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Evaluating pointer iterator </a:doc/a:elem> expected:<[/a:doc[1]/a:elem[1], /a:doc[1]/a:elem[2]]> but was:<[/a:doc[1]/a:elem[1], /a:doc[1]/a:elem[1]]>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMNodePointer\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMNodePointer\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: JXPathContext.iteratePointers() does not work with multiple prefixes for a single namespace URI\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Resolved | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nHave a look at the following document:\n\n<a:doc xmlns:a=\"ns\">\n  <a:elem />\n  <b:elem xmlns:b=\"ns\" />\n</a:doc>\n\nWe have two elements 'elem' in the same namespace 'ns'.\nThey have a different prefix, however.\n\nWhen we use JXPathContext.iteratePointers() to iterate over them, the first element is returned two times. The second element is not returned.\n\nThis is because\nin class org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMNodePointer\nin method getRelativePositionByName() (line 546)\nwe have:\n\nif (nm.equals(node.getNodeName()))\n\nIn the example, we have\nnm  == \"a:elem\" and node == \"b:elem\"\n\nThus, equals() returns false. But since 'a' and 'b' are just different prefixes for the same namespace URI, we should have 'true'.\n\nI attached a testcase which reproduces the bug.\n\nComments:\n\n[Christian Koppen]: A testcase which reproduces the bug\n\n[Christian Koppen]: Typo in the summary\n\n[Matthew Jason Benson]: Please test whether this problem is exhibited with the just-released JXPath 1.3.  Thanks!\n\n[Christian Koppen]: Problem also occurs in 1.3\n\n[Matthew Jason Benson]: After much delay...\n\nCommitted revision 917007.\n\nThanks!",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMNodePointer (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMNodePointer (fixed)\n@@ -557,17 +557,21 @@\n         int count = 1;\n         Node n = node.getPreviousSibling();\n         while (n != null) {\n-            if (n.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {\n-                String nm = n.getNodeName();\n-                if (nm.equals(node.getNodeName())) {\n+            if (n.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE && matchesQName(n)) {\n                 count++;\n-                }\n             }\n             n = n.getPreviousSibling();\n         }\n         return count;\n     }\n \n+    private boolean matchesQName(Node n) {\n+        if (getNamespaceURI() != null) {\n+            return equalStrings(getNamespaceURI(n), getNamespaceURI())\n+                    && equalStrings(node.getLocalName(), n.getLocalName());\n+        }\n+        return equalStrings(node.getNodeName(), n.getNodeName());\n+    }\n \n     /**\n      * Get relative position of this among all siblings.\n\n--- org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMNodePointer (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMNodePointer (fixed)\n@@ -693,8 +693,7 @@\n             String name = ((Element) node).getQualifiedName();\n             for (int i = 0; i < children.size(); i++) {\n                 Object child = children.get(i);\n-                if ((child instanceof Element)\n-                    && ((Element) child).getQualifiedName().equals(name)) {\n+                if (child instanceof Element && matchesQName(((Element) child))) {\n                     count++;\n                 }\n                 if (child == node) {\n@@ -706,6 +705,15 @@\n         return 1;\n     }\n \n+    private boolean matchesQName(Element element) {\n+        if (getNamespaceURI() != null) {\n+            String ns = getNamespaceURI(element);\n+            if (ns == null || !ns.equals(getNamespaceURI())) {\n+                return false;\n+            }\n+        }\n+        return element.getName().equals(((Element) node).getName());\n+    }\n \n     /**\n      * Get relative position of this among all siblings."
}